=== doublestar-prefix-name
--- .gitignore
**/node_modules/
**/target/*.jar
--- paths
node_modules
node_modules/
node_modules/pkg/index.js
web/node_modules/
web/app/node_modules/left-pad/index.js
target/a.jar
mod/target/a.jar
mod/target/classes/a.jar
mod/target/b.txt

=== escaped-slash-after-doublestar
--- .gitignore
a/**\/b
--- paths
a/b
a/x/b
a/**/b

=== doublestar-after-a-literal-prefix-is-a-plain-star
## git before 2.52 let "foo**/bar" match "foobar" (the literal prefix was cut off before wildmatch, so the "**"
## looked like the start of the pattern). 2.52 fixed it; this implementation follows the fixed behaviour.
min-git: 2.52
--- .gitignore
foo**/bar
a/b**/c
--- paths
foobar
a/bc
a/b/c
a/bx/c

=== doublestar-before-an-escaped-slash-spans-directories
## "**" as a whole component before an escaped slash is any run of bytes, slashes included: at least one directory
## sits between, so "x/b" does not match. An escaped slash also starts a component for a following "**".
--- .gitignore
x/**\/b
**\/c
v\/**\/d
--- paths
x/b
x/a/b
x/a/y/b
c
a/c
a/y/c
v/d
v/a/d
v/a/y/d

=== doublestar-before-an-escaped-letter-is-a-plain-star
--- .gitignore
x/**\b
--- paths
x/b
x/ab
x/a/b
x/a/cb
